# Internal-only survey content (never publish to public site)
#
# 3.xxx = commercial SaaS comparisons. Held for a reason that does not expire:
# publishing them makes us the arbiter of commercial software, which is not a
# role we want. This line stays.
#
# 2.xxx = protocol and standards surveys. Opened 2026-08-24 by allowlist. A
# standard is a public artifact being described, not a vendor being ranked, so
# the 3.xxx reasoning does not carry over — and 1.200 already points readers at
# "2.074 MCP Protocol" with nothing to reach. Denied by default and named one at
# a time, so the nine unfinished 2.xxx stubs and anything held cannot ride along:
# the series has 14 directories and only 4 completed surveys.
#
# NOTE: this file is the real enforcement, not publish_to_public.sh's
# --include='1-*.md' glob. A survey whose metadata.yaml claims a hold is not
# actually held unless publication: matches HELD_PUBLICATION_VALUES in
# convert_research.py — 2.078 carried a prose "INTERNAL ONLY" sentence that
# enforced nothing, and was kept off the site by this line alone.
content/survey/2-*.md
!content/survey/2-074.md
!content/survey/2-083.md
content/survey/3-*.md
